From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:20:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ceos: give cEOS pods the same soft placement KNE gives every
 container pod

MEASURED 2026-09-23 on DemoEstate (user-skyforge-demo-estate-13-fu-798b2b0d):
all 63 of its cEOS pods -- and all 72 cEOS pods cluster-wide -- sat on
worker-a, while the same lab's KNE-built pods spread
101/33/34/33 across worker-a and sm-node-b/c/d. The operator-built cEOS pod
spec carried `affinity` and `topologySpreadConstraints` both empty and only
the skyforge.example.com/labs=true nodeSelector, so the scheduler's
default scoring sent every cEOS to the node with the most allocatable CPU
(95 cores vs 30). That node is also the only disk-class=ssd node -- the one
kne 0058 reserves for KubeVirt VMs that must unpack ~28 GB on first boot --
and the node whose cilium endpoint count kne 0062 showed throttling pod
creation for the whole lab.

A KNE-built IOL pod in the same lab carries (kubectl get pod
siteA-bldg1-ios-csw01 -o jsonpath='{.spec.affinity}'):

  nodeAffinity.preferred[weight 100]:
      skyforge.example.com/disk-class NotIn [ssd]      (kne 0063)
  podAntiAffinity.preferred[weight 100]:
      topo In [<namespace>], topologyKey kubernetes.io/hostname (kne 0059/0062)

cEOS pods are built by this operator, not by KNE's CreatePod or its four
vendor copies, so none of kne 0059/0062/0063 ever reached them -- a sixth
pod-building site the same fix class missed.

getPod now sets pod.Spec.Affinity from getSkyforgeSoftPlacement(), which
renders exactly those two terms:

- SSD-avoid, from SKYFORGE_KNE_IO_HEAVY_NODE_LABELS_JSON -- the SAME policy
  input kne 0058 (VMs onto) and 0063 (containers away) read, NotIn per label
  in sorted key order in one preferred term, weight 100. Read from the
  device's envvars first (the path every getSkyforgePlacement input takes;
  kne 0024 forwards them in arista.CreateCRD) and then the operator's
  process env. Fails open: unset, blank, `{}` or unparseable -> no node
  affinity.
- Same-lab spread on `topo`, weight 100, topologyKey kubernetes.io/hostname.
  The value is read from the label map getPod stamps on this very pod, so
  selector and label agree by construction (the kne 0059 defect was a
  selector on a value no pod carried). getLabels() defaults topo to the
  namespace -- the value KNE's own pods carry -- so cEOS and IOL of one lab
  repel each other, not just their own kind. Unconditional, as in KNE.

PREFERRED ONLY, NEVER REQUIRED: a lab must never fail to schedule because
the preferred node is full, cordoned or absent.

NEW PODS ONLY. Reconcile's drift chain (configmap status, labels, env,
image, resources, args, init args/image, services, startup-probe agents)
never compares Affinity, so rolling this operator deletes and recreates
nothing; a running lab keeps its placement until its pods are recreated for
some other reason (stop/start, redeploy, a real drift). Labels ARE compared,
but getLabels() is unchanged, so no in-place label update fires either.

TESTS (controllers/ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go), written against
getPod/Reconcile only so the file compiles on the pre-change operator:
- TestGetPodSoftPlacementMatchesLiveKNEContainerPod: DeepEqual against the
  live IOL affinity JSON copied from the cluster, not a hand-written copy.
- TestGetPodSoftPlacementIsNeverRequired.
- TestGetPodSoftPlacementSelectorMatchesOwnTopoLabel: selector matches the
  pod's own labels, with and without KNE's CR labels.
- TestGetPodSoftPlacementNodePolicySources: unset/blank/{}/malformed fail
  open; operator env; device env; device `{}` overrides operator env.
  Positive control: all four FAIL on the 0001-0018 operator ("got
  (*v1.Affinity)(nil)") and pass with this patch.
- TestReconcileDoesNotRecreateRunningPodForAffinity: drives Reconcile on a
  fake client holding a pod with Affinity nil (a pre-change pod) after the
  policy is set; the pod survives five reconciles with its marker annotation
  and nil affinity, and the device reaches state "success" (the end of the
  drift chain, so survival is not an early return). In-harness positive
  control: an image change deletes the pod. Mutation control: inserting an
  Affinity DeepEqual drift check into Reconcile makes it FAIL ("running pod
  was RECREATED (marker lost)").

NOT PROVEN HERE: that cEOS pods actually land off worker-a. A preference ranks,
it does not guarantee. The check is the next DemoEstate bring-up.

WIRING: the operator Deployment carries only SKYFORGE_MAX_CONCURRENT_BRINGUP
today, so the SSD-avoid half stays dormant (fail-open) until either the
chart passes SKYFORGE_KNE_IO_HEAVY_NODE_LABELS_JSON to the manager
container or kne's arista.CreateCRD forwards it into the device envvars.
The same-lab spread needs no wiring.
---
 controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go       | 124 ++++++++
 .../ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go      | 275 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 399 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 controllers/ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go

diff --git a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
index 0e6ea06..432e306 100644
--- a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
+++ b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_controller.go
@@ -1192,6 +1192,127 @@ func getSkyforgePlacement(env map[string]string) (map[string]string, []corev1.To
 	return selector, tolerations, strings.TrimSpace(env["SKYFORGE_KNE_PRIORITY_CLASS_NAME"]), nil
 }
 
+const (
+	// ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv is the SAME policy input KNE reads for both halves of
+	// its IO-heavy placement (kne 0058 KNEIOHeavyNodeAffinity steers KubeVirt VMs
+	// ONTO the labelled nodes, kne 0063 KNEContainerNodeAffinity steers container
+	// pods AWAY from them). One input, so cEOS and the rest of the lab can never
+	// be steered by two different ideas of which node is "the SSD node".
+	ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv = "SKYFORGE_KNE_IO_HEAVY_NODE_LABELS_JSON"
+	// kneTopoLabel is the label KNE puts on every pod of a lab (value: the lab
+	// namespace) and that getLabels() puts on every cEOS pod by default.
+	kneTopoLabel = "topo"
+	// softPlacementWeight matches KNE's container-pod terms exactly (kne 0059/
+	// 0062 anti-affinity, kne 0063 node affinity), so a cEOS pod and an IOL pod
+	// of the same lab are ranked by the same rule with the same strength.
+	softPlacementWeight = 100
+)
+
+// getSkyforgeSoftPlacement gives a cEOS pod the SAME two soft placement terms
+// KNE gives every other container-backed lab pod (generic CreatePod plus the
+// cisco/juniper/forward/alpine copies). MEASURED 2026-09-23 on DemoEstate
+// (user-skyforge-demo-estate-13-fu-798b2b0d): every one of its 63 cEOS pods,
+// and all 72 cluster-wide, sat on worker-a, while its IOL/linux
+// pods spread 101/33/34/33 across the four lab nodes. The cEOS pod spec had
+// `affinity` and `topologySpreadConstraints` both empty and only the
+// skyforge.example.com/labs=true selector, so default scoring sent
+// every cEOS to the node with the most allocatable CPU (95 vs 30) -- which is
+// also the only disk-class=ssd node, the one kne 0058 reserves for the
+// KubeVirt VMs that must unpack ~28 GB on first boot.
+//
+// Rendered, the result is identical to a live KNE-built IOL pod's affinity:
+//
+//	nodeAffinity.preferred[weight 100]: <label> NotIn [<value>]  (per ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv entry)
+//	podAntiAffinity.preferred[weight 100]: topo In [<namespace>], topologyKey kubernetes.io/hostname
+//
+// PREFERRED ONLY, NEVER REQUIRED. Same contract as kne 0058/0063/0064: a lab
+// must never fail to schedule because the preferred node is full, cordoned or
+// absent. A preference ranks; it cannot refuse.
+//
+// THE ANTI-AFFINITY SELECTS THE LABEL THE POD ACTUALLY CARRIES. kne 0059/0062
+// exist because upstream KNE labelled pods topo=<namespace> and selected
+// topo In [<pod name>] -- a term that matched nothing, eleven lines apart.
+// Here the value is read from the label map getPod stamps on this very pod,
+// so the selector and the label agree by construction. getLabels() defaults
+// topo to the namespace, which is exactly the value KNE's own pods carry, so
+// cEOS and IOL of one lab repel EACH OTHER, not just their own kind.
+//
+// FAILS OPEN on the node half: an unset, empty, `{}` or unparseable policy
+// yields no node affinity (the anti-affinity is unconditional, as in KNE).
+// The policy is read from the device's envvars first -- the path every other
+// placement input in getSkyforgePlacement takes (kne 0024 forwards them from
+// the kne_cli env in arista.CreateCRD) -- and then from the operator's own
+// process env, so either wiring works and a per-device value is authoritative.
+//
+// NEW PODS ONLY. Pod affinity is not in the Reconcile drift checks (and is
+// immutable on a scheduled pod anyway), so rolling an operator that carries
+// this recreates nothing: a running lab keeps its placement until its pods are
+// recreated for some other reason (stop/start, redeploy, a real drift).
+func getSkyforgeSoftPlacement(podLabels map[string]string, env map[string]string) *corev1.Affinity {
+	affinity := &corev1.Affinity{NodeAffinity: getIOHeavyAvoidNodeAffinity(env)}
+	if topo := podLabels[kneTopoLabel]; topo != "" {
+		affinity.PodAntiAffinity = &corev1.PodAntiAffinity{
+			PreferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution: []corev1.WeightedPodAffinityTerm{{
+				Weight: softPlacementWeight,
+				PodAffinityTerm: corev1.PodAffinityTerm{
+					LabelSelector: &metav1.LabelSelector{
+						MatchExpressions: []metav1.LabelSelectorRequirement{{
+							Key:      kneTopoLabel,
+							Operator: metav1.LabelSelectorOpIn,
+							Values:   []string{topo},
+						}},
+					},
+					TopologyKey: "kubernetes.io/hostname",
+				},
+			}},
+		}
+	}
+	if affinity.NodeAffinity == nil && affinity.PodAntiAffinity == nil {
+		return nil
+	}
+	return affinity
+}
+
+// getIOHeavyAvoidNodeAffinity is the operator-side twin of kne 0063's
+// KNEContainerNodeAffinity: the complement (NotIn) of the IO-heavy node labels,
+// one expression per label in sorted key order, in ONE preferred term.
+func getIOHeavyAvoidNodeAffinity(env map[string]string) *corev1.NodeAffinity {
+	raw := strings.TrimSpace(env[ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv])
+	if raw == "" {
+		raw = strings.TrimSpace(os.Getenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv))
+	}
+	if raw == "" {
+		return nil
+	}
+	labels := map[string]string{}
+	if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(raw), &labels); err != nil {
+		kLog.Log.Error(err, "ignoring invalid "+ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnv+"; cEOS pods get no node preference")
+		return nil
+	}
+	if len(labels) == 0 {
+		return nil
+	}
+	keys := make([]string, 0, len(labels))
+	for k := range labels {
+		keys = append(keys, k)
+	}
+	sort.Strings(keys)
+	exprs := make([]corev1.NodeSelectorRequirement, 0, len(keys))
+	for _, k := range keys {
+		exprs = append(exprs, corev1.NodeSelectorRequirement{
+			Key:      k,
+			Operator: corev1.NodeSelectorOpNotIn,
+			Values:   []string{labels[k]},
+		})
+	}
+	return &corev1.NodeAffinity{
+		PreferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution: []corev1.PreferredSchedulingTerm{{
+			Weight:     softPlacementWeight,
+			Preference: corev1.NodeSelectorTerm{MatchExpressions: exprs},
+		}},
+	}
+}
+
 // Pods
 
 func getPod(pod *corev1.Pod, device *ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice, secretsAndConfigMaps map[string]client.Object, useStartupPersistence bool) error {
@@ -1279,6 +1400,9 @@ func getPod(pod *corev1.Pod, device *ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice, secretsAndCo
 		Tolerations:        tolerations,
 		PriorityClassName:  priorityClassName,
 		Volumes:            volumes,
+		// Soft placement parity with KNE's container pods. Preferred only, and
+		// not in the drift checks, so only newly created pods get it.
+		Affinity: getSkyforgeSoftPlacement(labels, envVarsMap),
 	}
 	return nil
 }
diff --git a/controllers/ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..578462d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/controllers/ceoslabdevice_soft_placement_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@
+package controllers
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"encoding/json"
+	"reflect"
+	"testing"
+
+	ceoslabv1alpha1 "github.com/aristanetworks/arista-ceoslab-operator/v2/api/v1alpha1"
+	corev1 "k8s.io/api/core/v1"
+	"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/errors"
+	metav1 "k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/apis/meta/v1"
+	"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels"
+	"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/runtime"
+	"k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/types"
+	ctrl "sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime"
+	"sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime/pkg/client/fake"
+)
+
+// These tests exercise getPod and Reconcile only -- no helper added by the
+// soft-placement change -- so the file compiles against the pre-change
+// operator and the parity tests FAIL there (positive control), then pass.
+
+const (
+	softPlacementNS     = "user-skyforge-demo-estate-13-fu-798b2b0d"
+	softPlacementPolicy = `{"skyforge.example.com/disk-class":"ssd"}`
+	// liveIOLAffinity is the affinity of a KNE-built IOL pod in the same lab,
+	// copied verbatim from the cluster on 2026-09-23:
+	//   kubectl -n user-skyforge-demo-estate-13-fu-798b2b0d get pod siteA-bldg1-ios-csw01 -o jsonpath='{.spec.affinity}'
+	liveIOLAffinity = `{"nodeAffinity":{"preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution":[{"preference":{"matchExpressions":[{"key":"skyforge.example.com/disk-class","operator":"NotIn","values":["ssd"]}]},"weight":100}]},"podAntiAffinity":{"preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution":[{"podAffinityTerm":{"labelSelector":{"matchExpressions":[{"key":"topo","operator":"In","values":["user-skyforge-demo-estate-13-fu-798b2b0d"]}]},"topologyKey":"kubernetes.io/hostname"},"weight":100}]}}`
+)
+
+// softPlacementDevice mirrors what KNE's arista node creates: the CR carries
+// topo=<namespace> plus model/os/vendor labels (read off the live
+// siteA-dc1-veos-leaf1 CEosLabDevice, 2026-09-23).
+func softPlacementDevice(env map[string]string) *ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice {
+	return &ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice{
+		ObjectMeta: metav1.ObjectMeta{
+			Name:      "siteA-dc1-veos-leaf1",
+			Namespace: softPlacementNS,
+			Labels: map[string]string{
+				"app": "siteA-dc1-veos-leaf1", "model": "ceos", "os": "eos",
+				"topo": softPlacementNS, "vendor": "ARISTA",
+			},
+		},
+		Spec: ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDeviceSpec{
+			Image:         "ceos:4.34.1F",
+			NumInterfaces: 2,
+			EnvVar:        env,
+		},
+	}
+}
+
+func buildSoftPlacementPod(t *testing.T, device *ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice) *corev1.Pod {
+	t.Helper()
+	pod := &corev1.Pod{}
+	if err := getPod(pod, device, nil, false); err != nil {
+		t.Fatalf("getPod() failed: %v", err)
+	}
+	return pod
+}
+
+// THE cEOS POD CARRIES EXACTLY WHAT KNE PUTS ON AN IOL POD OF THE SAME LAB.
+// Compared against the LIVE rendered IOL affinity rather than a hand-written
+// expectation, so "same soft placement as KNE" is checked against KNE's
+// actual output, not against our reading of it.
+func TestGetPodSoftPlacementMatchesLiveKNEContainerPod(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, softPlacementPolicy)
+	pod := buildSoftPlacementPod(t, softPlacementDevice(nil))
+
+	want := &corev1.Affinity{}
+	if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(liveIOLAffinity), want); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	if !reflect.DeepEqual(pod.Spec.Affinity, want) {
+		got, _ := json.Marshal(pod.Spec.Affinity)
+		t.Fatalf("cEOS affinity does not match the live KNE IOL pod\n got: %s\nwant: %s", got, liveIOLAffinity)
+	}
+}
+
+// NEVER REQUIRED: a lab must never fail to schedule because a preferred node
+// is full or absent. Pinned separately so a future "just make it required"
+// fails with the reason attached.
+func TestGetPodSoftPlacementIsNeverRequired(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, softPlacementPolicy)
+	a := buildSoftPlacementPod(t, softPlacementDevice(nil)).Spec.Affinity
+	if a == nil || a.NodeAffinity == nil || a.PodAntiAffinity == nil {
+		t.Fatalf("expected both soft terms, got %#v", a)
+	}
+	if a.NodeAffinity.RequiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution != nil {
+		t.Fatal("node affinity is REQUIRED -- a busy SSD node would refuse the lab")
+	}
+	if len(a.PodAntiAffinity.RequiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution) != 0 {
+		t.Fatal("pod anti-affinity is REQUIRED -- a lab larger than the node count would never schedule")
+	}
+	if a.PodAffinity != nil {
+		t.Fatalf("unexpected pod affinity %#v", a.PodAffinity)
+	}
+}
+
+// THE SELECTOR MUST SELECT THE POD'S OWN LABEL (the kne 0059/0062 defect: a
+// term keyed on a value no pod carries repels nothing). Checked against the
+// labels getPod actually stamped, for a CR whose topo label is present and
+// for one without any labels (getLabels defaults topo to the namespace).
+func TestGetPodSoftPlacementSelectorMatchesOwnTopoLabel(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, "")
+	bare := softPlacementDevice(nil)
+	bare.Labels = nil
+	for name, device := range map[string]*ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice{
+		"kne-labelled": softPlacementDevice(nil),
+		"unlabelled":   bare,
+	} {
+		t.Run(name, func(t *testing.T) {
+			pod := buildSoftPlacementPod(t, device)
+			if pod.Spec.Affinity == nil || pod.Spec.Affinity.PodAntiAffinity == nil {
+				t.Fatalf("no pod anti-affinity: %#v", pod.Spec.Affinity)
+			}
+			terms := pod.Spec.Affinity.PodAntiAffinity.PreferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution
+			if len(terms) != 1 || terms[0].Weight != 100 || terms[0].PodAffinityTerm.TopologyKey != "kubernetes.io/hostname" {
+				t.Fatalf("anti-affinity terms = %#v", terms)
+			}
+			sel, err := metav1.LabelSelectorAsSelector(terms[0].PodAffinityTerm.LabelSelector)
+			if err != nil {
+				t.Fatal(err)
+			}
+			if !sel.Matches(labels.Set(pod.Labels)) {
+				t.Fatalf("selector %q does not select the pod's own labels %v -- the term repels nothing", sel, pod.Labels)
+			}
+			if pod.Labels["topo"] != softPlacementNS {
+				t.Fatalf("topo label = %q, want the namespace %q (the value KNE's own pods carry)", pod.Labels["topo"], softPlacementNS)
+			}
+		})
+	}
+}
+
+// FAIL OPEN: no/empty/malformed policy -> no node affinity (the anti-affinity
+// is unconditional, as in KNE). A per-device envvar is authoritative over the
+// operator env, including a `{}` that disables it for that device.
+func TestGetPodSoftPlacementNodePolicySources(t *testing.T) {
+	for _, tc := range []struct {
+		name, processEnv string
+		deviceEnv        map[string]string
+		wantAvoidSSD     bool
+	}{
+		{name: "unset", processEnv: ""},
+		{name: "blank", processEnv: "   "},
+		{name: "empty object", processEnv: "{}"},
+		{name: "malformed", processEnv: "{not json"},
+		{name: "operator env", processEnv: softPlacementPolicy, wantAvoidSSD: true},
+		{name: "device env only", deviceEnv: map[string]string{ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest: softPlacementPolicy}, wantAvoidSSD: true},
+		{name: "device env disables", processEnv: softPlacementPolicy, deviceEnv: map[string]string{ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest: "{}"}},
+	} {
+		t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {
+			t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, tc.processEnv)
+			a := buildSoftPlacementPod(t, softPlacementDevice(tc.deviceEnv)).Spec.Affinity
+			if a == nil || a.PodAntiAffinity == nil {
+				t.Fatalf("pod anti-affinity must be unconditional, got %#v", a)
+			}
+			if !tc.wantAvoidSSD {
+				if a.NodeAffinity != nil {
+					t.Fatalf("expected no node affinity (fail open), got %#v", a.NodeAffinity)
+				}
+				return
+			}
+			if a.NodeAffinity == nil {
+				t.Fatal("expected the SSD-avoid node preference")
+			}
+			terms := a.NodeAffinity.PreferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution
+			want := []corev1.PreferredSchedulingTerm{{Weight: 100, Preference: corev1.NodeSelectorTerm{
+				MatchExpressions: []corev1.NodeSelectorRequirement{{
+					Key: "skyforge.example.com/disk-class", Operator: corev1.NodeSelectorOpNotIn, Values: []string{"ssd"},
+				}},
+			}}}
+			if !reflect.DeepEqual(terms, want) {
+				t.Fatalf("node affinity terms = %#v", terms)
+			}
+		})
+	}
+}
+
+// ROLLING THE OPERATOR MUST NOT RECREATE A RUNNING cEOS POD. Drive Reconcile
+// against a fake API server holding a pod shaped like one the pre-change
+// operator created (Affinity nil), with the SSD policy now set so the desired
+// affinity differs from the running pod's as much as it can. The pod must
+// survive every reconcile untouched. POSITIVE CONTROL in the same harness: a
+// real drift (an image change) is seen and the pod IS deleted, so a survival
+// here is not the harness failing to observe deletes.
+func TestReconcileDoesNotRecreateRunningPodForAffinity(t *testing.T) {
+	scheme := runtime.NewScheme()
+	if err := corev1.AddToScheme(scheme); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	if err := ceoslabv1alpha1.AddToScheme(scheme); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	ctx := context.Background()
+	device := softPlacementDevice(nil)
+	key := types.NamespacedName{Name: device.Name, Namespace: device.Namespace}
+	r := &CEosLabDeviceReconciler{
+		Client: fake.NewClientBuilder().WithScheme(scheme).WithObjects(device).Build(),
+		Scheme: scheme,
+	}
+	defer bringupAdmissions.release(key)
+	reconcileN := func(n int) {
+		t.Helper()
+		for i := 0; i < n; i++ {
+			if _, err := r.Reconcile(ctx, ctrl.Request{NamespacedName: key}); err != nil {
+				t.Fatalf("Reconcile #%d: %v", i, err)
+			}
+		}
+	}
+
+	// 1. The operator creates the pod, with no policy configured.
+	t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, "")
+	reconcileN(5)
+	pod := &corev1.Pod{}
+	if err := r.Get(ctx, key, pod); err != nil {
+		t.Fatalf("operator did not create the pod: %v", err)
+	}
+
+	// 2. Make it a PRE-CHANGE pod: no affinity at all, and a marker that a
+	//    delete+recreate would not carry over.
+	pod.Spec.Affinity = nil
+	if pod.Annotations == nil {
+		pod.Annotations = map[string]string{}
+	}
+	pod.Annotations["test/generation"] = "original"
+	if err := r.Update(ctx, pod); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+
+	// 3. Roll to an operator with the policy set; reconcile repeatedly.
+	t.Setenv(ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest, softPlacementPolicy)
+	reconcileN(5)
+	after := &corev1.Pod{}
+	if err := r.Get(ctx, key, after); err != nil {
+		t.Fatalf("running pod was DELETED on reconcile after the affinity change: %v", err)
+	}
+	if after.Annotations["test/generation"] != "original" {
+		t.Fatalf("running pod was RECREATED (marker lost): %v", after.Annotations)
+	}
+	if after.Spec.Affinity != nil {
+		t.Fatalf("running pod's affinity was rewritten in place: %#v", after.Spec.Affinity)
+	}
+	// Survival only counts if Reconcile walked the WHOLE drift chain and did
+	// not bail out early: "success" is set only after the last drift check.
+	reconciled := &ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice{}
+	if err := r.Get(ctx, key, reconciled); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	if reconciled.Status.State != SUCCESS_STATE {
+		t.Fatalf("Reconcile never reached the end of the drift checks (state=%q, reason=%q) -- survival proves nothing",
+			reconciled.Status.State, reconciled.Status.Reason)
+	}
+
+	// 4. Positive control: a real drift IS acted on by this same harness.
+	current := &ceoslabv1alpha1.CEosLabDevice{}
+	if err := r.Get(ctx, key, current); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	current.Spec.Image = "ceos:4.35.0F"
+	if err := r.Update(ctx, current); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	if _, err := r.Reconcile(ctx, ctrl.Request{NamespacedName: key}); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	if err := r.Get(ctx, key, &corev1.Pod{}); !errors.IsNotFound(err) {
+		t.Fatalf("positive control: an image change must delete the pod, got err=%v", err)
+	}
+}
+
+// Spelled out here rather than referencing the production constant so this
+// file compiles against the pre-change operator (the positive control).
+const ioHeavyNodeLabelsEnvForTest = "SKYFORGE_KNE_IO_HEAVY_NODE_LABELS_JSON"
